From 02004e002313b465ad67c1ba02cdb037c19d2f38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HR_Z <2463882771@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:02:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] PORT: report whether EFI_USBFN_IO_PROTOCOL exists at
 BDS time

First step of the USB bring-up on the GUI-capable baseline (7ccd7f42).

The architectural protocol fix in that commit finally publishes
gEfiResetArchProtocolGuid and gEfiSecurityArchProtocolGuid. GpiDxe, HALIOMMU and
UsbfnDwc3Dxe all DEPEX on the full architectural set, so they should dispatch for
the first time - and EFI_USBFN_IO_PROTOCOL being present is the direct evidence.

Printed through SerialPortWrite rather than ConOut: USB-related messages are
already known to survive on top of the Mu UI, whereas ConOut output does not.
---
 MdeModulePkg/Universal/BdsDxe/BdsEntry.c | 2882 +++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 1456 insertions(+), 1426 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Universal/BdsDxe/BdsEntry.c b/MdeModulePkg/Universal/BdsDxe/BdsEntry.c
index fa969c1..809b5b1 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Universal/BdsDxe/BdsEntry.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Universal/BdsDxe/BdsEntry.c
@@ -1,1426 +1,1456 @@
